    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0200" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3697: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan (Forbes) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-29T17:00:00+09:00">January 29, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 29—7:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. The Belgian Ambassador has frequently called upon me recently and expresses
                    great anxiety over the situation. He feels the Japanese Army has got out of
                    control, our dealings diplomatically being with a branch of the Government
                    [apparent garble] and with no power either of telling what the military and
                    naval branches of the Government <pb facs="0201" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/> are
                    going to do or of making them conform to any representations it may make. He
                    foresees additional trouble and is keeping in constant touch with me.</p>
                <p>The British Ambassador is also in touch with me and under instructions from his
                    Government is visiting the Foreign Office this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Our Naval Attaché has received an official account from the Japanese Navy
                    Department of events so far. They state that the landing of Japanese forces was
                    with an understanding with the Shanghai municipal authorities, as indicated in
                    my telegram No. 26, January 28, 9 p.m.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d117-f1"/> to
                    protect Japanese residents outside of Settlement zone. He is wiring details of
                    sharp clash with Chinese Regular Army, and reports additional Japanese cruiser
                    and four destroyers are being sent to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
